;; What THIS repository reaches into the shared security package for.
;;
;; Narrowed on 2026-08-21 when the decision plane moved to kotoba-lang/grant
;; (root ADR-2608219500). `aiueos.policy` and `aiueos.audit` were the entries
;; that used abac, crypto-policy, hardware, information-flow, transport and
;; redaction, and both left. What remains here is a handful of entrypoints
;; using a handful of controls.
;;
;; The six controls did not stop being exercised -- most are exercised in
;; grant now. Grant has no adoption record of its own yet, because the checker
;; that reads this one (`aiueos.tcb`) stayed with the machine. That gap is
;; named in root ADR-2608219500 rather than papered over by leaving stale
;; entrypoints here: a record that lists namespaces this repository no longer
;; contains would pass nothing and claim everything.
;;
;; adoption/version 3 (security pin 74235d1c) additionally requires the
;; `:sensitive-operations` inventory: every def/defn under src/ whose name
;; matches the verifier's sensitive-name pattern, each naming the shared
;; control that owns its decision. Both inventories below were computed from
;; source (kotoba.security.adoption/source-security-inventory and
;; source-sensitive-inventory), not written by hand; the entrypoint
;; namespaces gained the matching `kotoba.security.*` :require so the
;; declared control edges match what source actually imports.
;;
;; Control assignments: authentication/credential handling and backup
;; restore are information-flow decisions (kotoba's own manifest maps
;; principal-identity and kagi-boundary there); network-profile
;; encrypt/decrypt is crypto-policy. Root ADR-2608219500 remains the owner
;; of any re-assignment.
{:adoption/version 3
 :consumer/id :aiueos
 :security/git-sha "fde703a1b2e5085d86f3c1fdf9b97558912e0275"
 :required-control-namespaces
 [kotoba.security.supply-chain kotoba.security.crypto-policy
  kotoba.security.information-flow]
 :security-sensitive-entrypoints
 {aiueos.reproducibility [kotoba.security.supply-chain]
  aiueos.device-auth [kotoba.security.information-flow]
  aiueos.phone-bind [kotoba.security.crypto-policy]
  aiueos.cloud-live [kotoba.security.information-flow]
  aiueos.sealed-state [kotoba.security.information-flow]}
 ;; Discovered by kotoba.security.adoption/source-sensitive-inventory, which
 ;; scans src/ (tree-seq, nested defns included) for def/defn names matching
 ;; its sensitive-name pattern. Each entry names the shared control that owns
 ;; its decision.
 :sensitive-operations
 {aiueos.device-auth/authenticate-account [kotoba.security.information-flow]
  aiueos.phone-bind/encrypt-network-profile [kotoba.security.crypto-policy]
  aiueos.phone-bind/decrypt-network-envelope [kotoba.security.crypto-policy]
  aiueos.cloud-live/credential [kotoba.security.information-flow]
  aiueos.sealed-state/restore-backup! [kotoba.security.information-flow]}
 :exceptions []}
